@startuml
title Cross-chain bridge — data flow and trust boundaries
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam componentBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam componentBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam packageBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam packageBorderColor #B54A4A
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF6F6
skinparam noteBorderColor #B54A4A
skinparam arrowColor #4A78B5
skinparam databaseBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam databaseBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam actorBorderColor #4A78B5
left to right direction

package "1. Origin chain" as P1 {
  actor "Bridge user" as USER
  [Escrow / LockProxy] as LOCK
  database "Locked balances" as ESC
}

package "1b. Origin-chain data path" as P1B {
  [Internal RPC nodes] as RPCI
  [External RPC provider] as RPCE
}

package "2. Off-chain attestation layer" as P2 {
  [Attestor set\nvalidators / keepers / DVNs] as SIG
  database "Signer private keys" as KEYS
  [Relay chain\n(optional)] as RELAY
  [Relayer (permissionless)] as REL
}

package "3. Target chain" as P3 {
  [Proxy + implementation] as PROXY
  [Gateway / verifier] as GW
  database "Processed message set" as NONCE
  database "Required verifier set\nand threshold" as CFG
}

package "Build and release" as P4 {
  [Source repository] as SRC
  [Compilation environment] as BUILD
}

package "Configuration" as P6 {
  actor "Application delegate" as APP
}

package "Detection and response" as P5 {
  [Reconciliation monitor] as MON
  [Pause / guardian] as PAUSE
}

USER -[#B54A4A]-> LOCK : lock or burn assets
LOCK --> ESC : credit escrow
LOCK --> RPCI : observable state
LOCK --> RPCE : observable state
RPCI -[#B54A4A]-> SIG : **TB1** claimed origin state
RPCE -[#B54A4A]-> SIG : **TB1** claimed origin state
KEYS --> SIG : sign with
SIG --> RELAY : commit state
RELAY --> REL : header + proof
SIG --> REL : threshold attestations
REL -[#B54A4A]-> GW : **TB2** withdrawal proof
CFG --> GW : how many must attest
GW --> NONCE : check and record
GW --> USER : release assets

SRC --> BUILD
BUILD -[#B54A4A]-> SIG : **TB4** node binary
PROXY -[#B54A4A]-> GW : **TB5** delegates to
APP -[#B54A4A]-> CFG : **TB2** sets required verifiers

LOCK --> MON
GW --> MON
MON --> PAUSE : halt on mismatch
PAUSE --> GW

note bottom of GW
  **TB2 is where every attack arrives.**
  The gateway counts attestations against a
  threshold and has no independent view of
  the origin chain.
  **TB1 is how it is reached without a key.**
  Poison enough of the data path and the
  honest attestor signs voluntarily
  (Kelp DAO 2026).
  TB3 (corporate IT to attestor host)
  sits inside package 2.
end note

note top of RPCE
  Redundancy here must **fail closed**.
  A DDoS on the honest source that
  triggers failover onto a poisoned one
  turns an availability attack into an
  integrity attack.
end note
@enduml
